  "english": "25. Tuesday. Tone 1 [AJ]. Vahan of Goghtn,\n- and Eugene the virgin, etc.\nHymn of the Fathers, Tone 1 [AK]: \"Who art exalted.\" 9.\n27. Thursday. Tone 2 [BZ]. Eugenios, Makarios,\netc. Fathers, Tone 2 [B2]: \"Without malice.\"\n29. Saturday. Tone 3 [GDZ]. Gregory the Theologian.\n30. Sunday. Tone 3 [GK]. Third [Sunday]. Fathers, Tone 3 [G3]: \"Creator of creatures.\" Dismissal [Hambartsi], Tone 3 [GK]: \"A vision lightning-like.\" 7.\nFor the things placed below, see the First Volume after\nVartavar [Transfiguration]; but look here for the Fathers and the tones. 24.\n31. Monday. Tone 4 [DZC]. Cyprian the Bishop,\netc. Fathers, Tone 4 [B3]: \"With your saints.\"\nFebruary 22.\n1. Tuesday. Tone 4 [DK]. Athenogenes the Bishop,\netc. Fathers, Tone 4 [BK]: \"We bless thee.\"\n2. Wednesday. Tone 1 [AZ]. Fathers of Lent, Tone 2 [BDZ]: \"Who art awesome.\"\n3. Thursday. Tone 1 [AK]. The Forefathers: Adam, Abel, etc.\n5. Saturday. Tone 2 [BK]. The Sons and Grandsons of Gregory the Illuminator. 3.\n6. Sunday. Tone 3 [GD]. Fourth [Sunday]. Fathers, Tone 3 [GK]: \"Today he is armed.\" Dismissal [Hambartsi], Tone 3 [G3]: \"In an awesome voice.\" 10.\n7. Monday. Tone 3 [GK]. The Maccabees, Eleazar,\netc. Fathers, Tone 4 [BK]: \"Who in battle.\" 24.\n8. Tuesday. Tone 4 [GD]. The Twelve Prophets: Hosea, etc. 4331.\n9. Wednesday. Tone 4 [DK]. Fathers of Lent, Tone 4 [BK]: \"Blessed art thou Lord, God of our fathers.\"\n10. Thursday. Tone 1 [AZ]. Sophia and her three daughters. Fathers, Tone 3 [G]: \"Who the torments.\"\n12. Saturday. Tone 2 [BZ]. Thaddeus the Apostle and Sandukht the virgin. 9.\n13. Sunday. Tone 2 [BK]. Fifth [Sunday]. Dismissal [Hambartsi], Tone 2 [BK]: \"The Resurrection of Christ.\"\nPre-Lenten Fast [Arachavorats] Eve.\n14. Monday. Tone 3 [GZ]. Fast. The Presentation of the Lord [Tearndaraj].\n15. Tuesday. Tone 3 [GK]. Fast. Fathers of Lent, Tone 4 [BK]: \"Lord God of our fathers.\"\n20. Sunday. Tone 2 [BZ]. Dismissal [Hambartsi], Tone 2 [BDZ]: \"The wonderful women.\"\n27. Sunday. Tone 1 [AK]. Mid-Lent [Mijink]. Fathers, Tone 4 [DK]: \"Who didst assume.\" Dismissal [Hambartsi], Tone 1 [AK]: \"We shall sing to thee with the angels.\" 24.\nMarch:\nSunday. Tone 4 [DK]. Great Eve of Lent [Bun Barekendan]. And see the others in order in the First Volume, keeping the order of the place.\n\nThursday. Tone 4 [DK]. Fast. Feast of the Annunciation of the Holy Virgin.\nSunday. Tone 1 [AZ]. Easter: Day of the Resurrection of Christ. See also the others in order in the First Volume.\nJune\nThursday. Tone 4 [DK]. Ascension of Christ.\nSunday. Tone 1 [AK]. Coming of the Holy Spirit [Pentecost]. Eve of the Fast of Elijah.\nSunday. Tone 1 [AZ]. First [Sunday]. Beginning of the Sundays of the Resurrection. Look here for the Fathers of these intervening Sundays.\nJuly\nSunday. Tone 4 [DZ]. Third [Sunday]. Fathers, Tone 1 [AK]: \"Who didst come for salvation.\"\nSunday. Tone 3 [GK]. Fourth [Sunday]. Fathers, Tone 2 [BDZ]: \"Who didst descend from heaven.\"\nSunday. Tone 2 [BK]. Sixth [Sunday]. Fathers, Tone 2 [BK]: \"Who art heavenly.\" Eve of the Fast of Vartavar [Transfiguration].\nSunday. Tone 2 [BZ]. Vartavar [Transfiguration]. The period of non-fasting days is one week. See the First Volume.\nAugust\nSaturday. Tone 1 [AZ]. The Holy Council of Ephesus of the two hundred Patriarchs.\nSunday. Tone 1 [AK]. Second [Sunday]. Fathers, Tone 3 [G3]: \"We glorify.\" Eve of the Fast of the Holy Mother of God.\nMonday. Tone 2 [BZC]. Fast. Fathers of Lent, Tone 1 [AK]: \"Glorified forever.\"\nSunday. Tone 1 [AZ]. Assumption of the Holy Mother of God. The period of non-fasting days is three weeks. See this intervening period in the First Volume, keeping the order of the place.\nWednesday. Tone 2 [BD]. Fathers, Tone 3 [G]: \"Who by thy awesome power.\"",
